From bbdc134006eb2222e525df1f70adbde4ea647191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:44:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the racer count on Rule Settings, alone too (first
 version, L/R)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Gibax (2026-11-26): "on est capable de choisir le nombre de racers/riders par
course. Faudrait ajouter cette option au jeu normal (même endroit qu'on ajuste
les laps etc) in game, pour du offline aussi".

- Rule Settings is the task 0x805A6660 (from Track Select 0x80534AC4, from
  the menus' 0x8050EDB8 in its state 22); its data's cursor at +30, count at
  +31 (8: six rows, Default, CONTINUE), values +32, maxima +38, minima +44,
  the rows' masks in the rules word at +0 (RAM dumps and its code,
  0x805A68C4). Seen from the menus' task: state 22, data +156 = 2.
- A "Racers" row is drawn under Air Lost (the waiting screen's overlay, now
  on every present, online or not), changed with L and R, which that menu
  leaves alone (measured), 1 to 8 (8: the game's). The host's count goes to
  the relay with the course and laps, as before.
- Alone, the count is written into the race the game sets up: the racer
  count stays 8 through the menus (measured: it never goes back to 1), the
  player count is set after Player Entry, loading screens follow until the
  race (scene 4); during those, the count (at least the players) and a CPU
  character for racers the menu left empty (4 made with 3 players or more).
  Measured: Rule Settings 5, a race of 5 (Sonic 5th).

Gibax wants it as a real row of the menu (the cursor on it, Default moved
beside CONTINUE, the menu's own font): next.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
